# TOEFL Reading — Day51

## Topic: Ecosystem Recovery

Ecosystems can sometimes recover after natural disasters or human disturbances. The speed of recovery depends on several factors, including the severity of the damage, the availability of resources, and the ability of organisms to adapt.

Some ecosystems recover naturally when plants and animals return to damaged areas. In other cases, humans may assist the recovery process by restoring habitats or reintroducing native species.

However, recovery is not always complete. If an ecosystem loses important species or experiences continuous disturbance, it may change into a different ecological system.

